        {
          "row_id": "r1",
          "col_id": "c1",
          "value_verbatim": "• Estimate the rates of hospital-acquired or ventilator-associated bacterial\npneumonia (HABP/VABP) developing in intensive care unit (ICU) patients\nconsidered high risk for pneumonia, as defined by treatment with one or\nmore of the following respiratory modalities for at least 12 hours, either\ncurrently or within the prior 7 days in patients age ≥18 year old (Arm 1)*:\n− Invasive mechanical ventilation\n− Noninvasive ventilation (bilevel positive airway pressure [BiPAP] or\ncontinuous positive airway pressure [CPAP] for any indication other\nthan obstructive sleep apnea)\n− High-flow, supplemental oxygen therapy via nasal cannula. Only\ninclude systems using an air/oxygen blender capable of delivering a\nprecise fraction of inspired oxygen [FiO2] level, not just a flow in\nliters per minute (LPM)\n− High flow supplemental oxygen therapy delivering at least 50% FiO2\nvia aerosol facemask or tracheostomy collar (mask). Only include\nsystems using an air/oxygen blender capable of delivering a precise\nFiO2 level, not just a flow in LPM.\n− Supplemental oxygen therapy delivered via either partial or non-\nrebreather face mask.\n* For patients age <18 year old (Arm 2), see Appendix B\n• Estimate the proportion of patients diagnosed with HABP/VABP who would\nbe eligible for enrollment in a clinical trial of antibacterial therapy for\nHABP/VABP per U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) draft guidance\ndocument criteria.",
          "shaded": false,
          "colspan": 1,
          "rowspan": 1,
          "footnote_markers": [
            "*",
            "•"
          ],
          "sup_markers": [],
          "page": 7,
          "bbox": [
            164.5,
            160.7,
            535.3,
            501.2
          ],
          "evidence": [
            "text_layer"
          ],
          "authored_by": "geometry",
          "ambiguous": false,
          "ambiguity_reason": null
        },
        {
          "row_id": "r2",
          "col_id": "c1",
          "value_verbatim": "Arm 1: Adult (≥18 years) patients admitted to ICUs\nArm 2: Pediatric (<18 years) patients admitted to ICUs or intermediate care unit",
          "shaded": false,
